1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Your seatbelt light won't turn off

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
— even after you buckle up.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,500
The belt clicks in fine.

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,000
The chime keeps going, or the icon stays lit anyway.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
That's usually the buckle switch —

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
a small sensor inside the receptacle, not the belt itself.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Wear, corrosion, or debris inside the buckle

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
can stop it from registering a good latch.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Always wear the belt regardless —

10
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,000
but a switch like that can point to a bigger electrical gremlin.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Worth checking it out.

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Stop by and we'll take a look — Nick's Tire & Auto.
